WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:06.544
The next morning the earl sat in a chair by the library window.

2
00:00:06.545 --> 00:00:12.482
Cedric stood nearby, impatiently waiting for his pony to arrive.

3
00:00:12.483 --> 00:00:19.425
Peering out the open window, Cedric spotted Wilkins, the head groom, leading the pony.

4
00:00:19.426 --> 00:00:24.261
A second groom followed with Wilkins' horse.

5
00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:29.196
"Here comes my pony!" Cedric shouted joyfully.

6
00:00:29.197 --> 00:00:35.573
"Oh, it's such a beautiful brown color! I can't wait to ride!"

7
00:00:35.574 --> 00:00:41.371
The earl almost smiled as his grandson dashed from the room.

8
00:00:41.372 --> 00:00:45.839
"That's not a small pony," the earl thought.

9
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.401
"I wonder how brave Cedric will be in the saddle."

10
00:00:51.402 --> 00:00:55.970
With the help of Wilkins, Cedric mounted his pony.

11
00:00:55.971 --> 00:01:02.300
Then Wilkins led the pony in a circle while the earl watched.

12
00:01:02.301 --> 00:01:06.258
"Am I sitting up straight, Wilkins?" Cedric asked.

13
00:01:06.259 --> 00:01:09.886
"The riders sit up straight at the circus."

14
00:01:09.887 --> 00:01:16.962
Wilkins smiled. "No one could sit up straighter, my lord."

15
00:01:16.963 --> 00:01:22.791
After a few more rounds, Wilkins and the earl were pleased with Cedric's progress.

16
00:01:22.792 --> 00:01:25.597
But Cedric wanted to do more.

17
00:01:25.598 --> 00:01:30.372
"Can I ride by myself, Grandpapa?" Cedric pleaded.

18
00:01:30.373 --> 00:01:38.080
"I want to go faster. In New York I used to see a boy trotting and galloping through the park."

19
00:01:38.081 --> 00:01:43.096
"Do you think you can handle trotting?" the earl asked.

20
00:01:43.097 --> 00:01:46.704
"It's not as easy as it looks."

21
00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:50.413
"I'd like to try," Cedric said.

22
00:01:50.414 --> 00:01:56.383
"All right. Wilkins, let his lordship try."

23
00:01:56.384 --> 00:02:02.438
Wilkins motioned for the other groom to bring over his horse.

24
00:02:02.439 --> 00:02:08.106
"Are you ready, your lordship?" Wilkins mounted his horse.

25
00:02:08.107 --> 00:02:11.747
"Ready!" Cedric shouted.

26
00:02:11.748 --> 00:02:15.308
The next few minutes were exciting ones for Cedric.

27
00:02:15.309 --> 00:02:20.426
He bounced in the saddle as Wilkins led his pony at a trot.

28
00:02:20.427 --> 00:02:24.803
Cedric was soon out of breath, and his face was red.

29
00:02:24.804 --> 00:02:28.670
But he still tried to sit up straight.

30
00:02:28.671 --> 00:02:34.998
"Trotting j-j-jolts you a g-g-good deal!" Cedric said.

31
00:02:34.999 --> 00:02:38.572
"You'll get used to it," Wilkins said.

32
00:02:38.573 --> 00:02:43.014
They went around a bend and disappeared from the earl's view.

33
00:02:43.015 --> 00:02:54.132
The earl chuckled. "I expect they'll be walking when they return."

34
00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:58.072
But the earl was surprised when Cedric rode into view.

35
00:02:58.073 --> 00:03:02.543
His hat was missing, and he was holding on for dear life.

36
00:03:02.544 --> 00:03:07.417
But he was still in the saddle, and he was still trotting.

37
00:03:07.418 --> 00:03:16.031
"Stop a minute!" the earl called out the window. "Where's your hat, Cedric?"

38
00:03:16.032 --> 00:03:20.454
"It fell off, your lordship," Wilkins answered for Cedric.

39
00:03:20.455 --> 00:03:24.281
"And he wouldn't let me pick it up."

40
00:03:24.282 --> 00:03:31.679
The earl continued talking to Wilkins. "His lordship's not afraid, is he?"

41
00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.864
"I don't think he knows the meaning of the word."

42
00:03:34.865 --> 00:03:38.733
Wilkins looked proudly at his pupil.

43
00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:41.909
"I've taught many young gentlemen to ride.

44
00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.853
I've never had one more determined to learn."

45
00:03:45.854 --> 00:03:53.482
The earl turned his attention to his grandson. "Are you tired? Do you want to get off?"

46
00:03:53.483 --> 00:04:00.648
"I'm a little tired," Cedric admitted. "But I don't want to get down.

47
00:04:00.649 --> 00:04:09.145
As soon as I catch my breath, I'll retrieve my hat. Are you ready, Wilkins?"

48
00:04:09.146 --> 00:04:13.753
As they trotted away, the earl's eyes gleamed with happiness.

49
00:04:13.754 --> 00:04:18.548
He couldn't remember the last time he'd felt like this.

50
00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:24.302
A few minutes later, the two riders returned at a gallop.

51
00:04:24.303 --> 00:04:29.429
"There!" Cedric was exhausted but triumphant.

52
00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:38.475
"I galloped! I didn't do it as well as the boy in New York. But I didn't fall off!"

53
00:04:38.476 --> 00:04:43.308
After that, Cedric went riding with Wilkins almost every day.

54
00:04:43.309 --> 00:04:50.449
Everyone in the countryside grew used to seeing Lord Fauntleroy on his brown pony.

55
00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:56.035
One afternoon Cedric noticed a boy limping home from the village school.

56
00:04:56.036 --> 00:05:01.231
"I'll walk, and he can ride my pony," Cedric said to Wilkins.

57
00:05:01.232 --> 00:05:06.416
Wilkins knew that a young gentleman shouldn't give up his pony for a villager.

58
00:05:06.417 --> 00:05:12.101
"No, I'll get down, and the boy can ride my horse."

59
00:05:12.102 --> 00:05:16.340
"But he might not feel comfortable on such a big animal."

60
00:05:16.341 --> 00:05:25.415
Before Wilkins could object, Cedric dismounted. "Besides I want to talk to him."

61
00:05:25.416 --> 00:05:31.080
The boy was too surprised to refuse Cedric's offer.

62
00:05:31.081 --> 00:05:37.087
When they reached his cottage, his mother came to the gate.

63
00:05:37.088 --> 00:05:41.038
"I've brought your son home, ma'am," Cedric said.

64
00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:43.498
"He could use some crutches.

65
00:05:43.499 --> 00:05:47.895
I'll ask my grandfather to have a pair made for him."

66
00:05:47.896 --> 00:05:53.010
Wilkins nervously watched the scene, wondering how he'd explain it.

67
00:05:53.011 --> 00:05:58.562
"The earl won't like this," he thought.

68
00:05:58.563 --> 00:06:02.728
But when the earl heard what happened, he wasn't angry.

69
00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:09.152
Instead he made Cedric tell him the story again.

70
00:06:09.153 --> 00:06:15.214
A few days later, Cedric delivered the crutches while the earl stayed in the carriage.

71
00:06:15.215 --> 00:06:20.086
When Cedric returned to the carriage, he was shaking his head in disbelief.

72
00:06:20.087 --> 00:06:25.141
"Grandpapa, it was just like when you helped Mary.

73
00:06:25.142 --> 00:06:29.568
The boy's mother was crying with happiness," he said.

74
00:06:29.569 --> 00:06:32.349
"I told her you sent the crutches.

75
00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:39.541
You didn't tell me to say that, but I thought maybe you forgot. That was right, wasn't it?"

76
00:06:39.542 --> 00:06:48.853
The earl laughed and didn't contradict his grandson.

